  "name": "no-printed-vp",
  "description": "A DIAGNOSTIC, NOT A PROPOSAL (Dean, 2026-08-09). Every printed VP in the corner of a card is set to 0, so a card can only be worth building for what its text does. Abilities, costs and thresholds are untouched, and the Endgame cards still score through their gameEnd text because that text IS their ability. The question it answers: are the upper tiers being built for their power or only for their 2 and 3 printed VP? Read the play rates and the activation counts, not the scores - with a fifth of the scoring removed the winning score is not comparable to the reference by construction. ⛔ PASSENGERS PINNED 12/09/2026: Dean's plain-action balloon and Village Store ruling moved sixteen shipped leaves at once. This overlay predates that flip and every report taken against it does too, so each of those leaves is pinned here BY NAME at its PRE-FLIP value. Without it an arm read as a delta against a pre-flip base would silently gain a one-card flight, an always-present Aerodrome and a live coin economy. That is the 05/09/2026 passenger lesson: an overlay that should not move with the shipped default has to pin every knob the flip moved.",
